{"abstract":[{"text":"Represent SMPTE timecode at any standard frame rate, and convert it to and from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an exact number of seconds.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"IvorSMPTE has four types:","type":"text"}]},{"alignments":["left","left"],"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Type","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Represents","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTEFrameRate","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One of the 12 standard SMPTE frame rates","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A timecode at a frame rate, to the hundredth of a frame","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTEExactSeconds","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An exact, non-negative number of seconds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETimeConverter","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A fixed mapping between seconds and timecode","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every time in IvorSMPTE is exact. The NTSC-derived frame rates are rational"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"numbers (29.97 frames per second is exactly 30000\/1001), and seconds are kept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as rational numbers too, so converting a timecode to seconds and back never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drifts."}]},{"text":"Frame rates","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Frame-rates"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTEFrameRate","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" has a case for each standard rate. The NTSC-derived rates —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"23.976, 29.97, and 59.94 — run at 1000\/1001 of their nominal rate, and 29.97,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"30, 59.94, and 60 each come in a non-drop-frame and a drop-frame form:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let rate = SMPTEFrameRate.fps2997Drop","","rate.isDropFrame    \/\/ true","rate.uintValue      \/\/ 30, the nominal rate: frame numbers per second","rate.numberValue    \/\/ 30000\/1001, the exact rate","rate.description    \/\/ \"29.97DF\"","","SMPTEFrameRate(string: \"23.98\")     \/\/ .fps23976"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drop-frame timecode skips frame numbers — 0 and 1 at 29.97 and 30 frames per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"second, 0 through 3 at 59.94 and 60 — at the start of every minute except"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minutes 0, 10, 20, 30, 40, and 50. At 29.97 and 59.94 frames per second this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps timecode in step with real time. The 30 and 60 frames per second"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drop-frame rates run at a true 30 or 60, so their timecode does not; they are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"typically used for material that is pulled down to 29.97 or 59.94 drop-frame."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTEFrameRate\/framesPerDay","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the number of frames in 24 hours of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timecode, which accounts for the skipped frame numbers."}]},{"text":"Timecodes","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Timecodes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is a frame rate together with hour, minute, second, frame, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subframe (hundredths of a frame) components. It can be made in four ways:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From its components, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime\/init(frameRate:hour:minute:second:frame:subframe:)","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HH:MM:SS:FF"},{"text":" string, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime\/init(string:frameRate:)","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"At drop-frame rates the separator before the frame number may be ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":";"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":":"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the string may end with a period and a two-digit subframe, as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"01:00:03;12.50"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From a number of frames since midnight, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime\/init(frameRate:frameCount:subframe:)","isActive":true},{"text":". At drop-frame rates the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"frames are numbered with drop-frame timecode.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From an exact number of seconds since midnight, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime\/init(frameRate:elapsedSeconds:)","isActive":true},{"text":", which rounds to the nearest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hundredth of a frame and wraps around after 24 hours.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The first three are failable, returning "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for any component out of range,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including a frame number that drop-frame timecode skips. The last never fails."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let time = SMPTETime(frameRate: .fps2997Drop,","                     frameCount: 1800,","                     subframe: 0)","","time?.description   \/\/ \"00:01:00;02\"","time?.frameCount    \/\/ 1800"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A timecode’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime\/description","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is its "},{"code":"HH:MM:SS:FF","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" string, with "},{"code":";","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before the frame number at drop-frame rates and a subframe suffix if it is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zero."}]},{"text":"Exact seconds","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Exact-seconds"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime\/elapsedSeconds","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a timecode’s exact time since midnight as an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTEExactSeconds","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", which holds a rational "},{"code":"Number","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/eBardX\/XestiNumbers","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTEExactSeconds","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" can be written as an integer, floating-point, or string"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"literal, or made from a "},{"code":"Number","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTEExactSeconds\/init(numberValue:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for a negative or non-finite number."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A floating-point value is converted to the exact rational value it represents,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is not always the decimal it looks like: "},{"code":"0.1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not exactly one tenth."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"To write a decimal fraction exactly, use "},{"code":"Number(numerator:denominator:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Changing frame rate","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Changing-frame-rate"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There are two ways to move a timecode to another frame rate, and they answer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"different questions:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Converting through seconds keeps the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"moment"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": make a new ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the old one’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime\/elapsedSeconds","isActive":true},{"text":" at the new rate.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime\/retimed(to:)","isActive":true},{"text":" keeps the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"label"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": 01:00:00:00 at 25 frames per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"second becomes 01:00:00:00 at any other rate. The frame number is clamped to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the new rate’s last frame, and at a drop-frame rate a skipped frame number","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"becomes the first one kept, so 00:01:00:00 at 30 frames per second becomes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"00:01:00;02 at 29.97 drop-frame.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"text":"Timecode conversion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Timecode-conversion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETimeConverter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" labels a timeline measured in seconds — the wall"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time of a performance, say — with timecode that starts at a chosen timecode."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Its frame rate is the start timecode’s:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let start     = SMPTETime(string: \"01:00:00:00\", frameRate: .fps25)!","let converter = SMPTETimeConverter(startTime: start)","","converter.smpteTime(at: 90)     \/\/ 01:01:30:00","","let earlier = SMPTETime(string: \"00:59:00:00\", frameRate: .fps25)!","","converter.seconds(at: earlier)  \/\/ 86340: the next day"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because timecode wraps around after 24 hours, a timecode earlier than the start"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timecode is taken to fall on the following day, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETimeConverter\/seconds(at:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" always returns at least zero and less than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one day. The timecode it is given must be at the converter’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETimeConverter\/frameRate","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Error handling","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Error-handling"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IvorSMPTE throws no errors. Every conversion that can fail returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead: the failable "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTEExactSeconds","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" initializers, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTEFrameRate\/init(string:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". Passing "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETimeConverter\/seconds(at:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timecode at a different frame rate from the converter’s is a programming error,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and stops execution."}]},{"text":"Concurrency","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Concurrency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IvorSMPTE is built for Swift 6 strict concurrency. Every public type is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value type, so instances can be freely shared across tasks and actor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundaries."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/UsingIvorSMPTE"},"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"IvorSMPTE"}],"title":"Using IvorSMPTE"},"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivorsmpte\/usingivorsmpte"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://IvorSMPTE/documentation/IvorSMPTE/SMPTEFrameRate/framesPerDay":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivorsmpte\/smpteframerate\/framesperday","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTEFrameRate\/framesPerDay","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"framesPerDay","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Su","text":"UInt","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"framesPerDay","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The number of frames in one day (24 hours) of timecode at this frame","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rate.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorSMPTE/documentation/IvorSMPTE/SMPTETime/retimed(to:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivorsmpte\/smptetime\/retimed(to:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime\/retimed(to:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"retimed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SMPTEFrameRate","preciseIdentifier":"s:9IvorSMPTE14SMPTEFrameRateO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SMPTETime","preciseIdentifier":"s:9IvorSMPTE9SMPTETimeV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"retimed(to:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Returns this timecode at a different frame rate, keeping its hour,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute, second, and subframe components.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorSMPTE/documentation/IvorSMPTE/SMPTETimeConverter/frameRate":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETimeConverter\/frameRate","title":"frameRate","url":"\/documentation\/ivorsmpte\/smptetimeconverter\/framerate","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"frameRate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SMPTEFrameRate","preciseIdentifier":"s:9IvorSMPTE14SMPTEFrameRateO","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The SMPTE frame rate of the timecodes this converter produces.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorSMPTE/documentation/IvorSMPTE/SMPTETime/init(string:frameRate:)":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivorsmpte\/smptetime\/init(string:framerate:)","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"SMPTETime","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance by parsing its string representation,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if the string cannot be parsed or any component is out of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range for the given frame rate.","type":"text"}],"title":"init(string:frameRate:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"?(","kind":"text"},{"text":"string","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"frameRate","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:9IvorSMPTE14SMPTEFrameRateO","text":"SMPTEFrameRate","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETime\/init(string:frameRate:)","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorSMPTE/documentation/IvorSMPTE/SMPTETime/init(frameRate:frameCount:subframe:)":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivorsmpte\/smptetime\/init(framerate:framecount:subframe:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"code":"SMPTETime","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance from a number of frames since"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"midnight (00:00:00:00), or "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if the frame count or subframe is out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of range for the given frame rate."}],"title":"init(frameRate:frameCount:subframe:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"?(","kind":"text"},{"text":"frameRate","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:9IvorSMPTE14SMPTEFrameRateO","text":"SMPTEFrameRate","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"frameCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Su","text":"UInt","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"subframe","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Su","text":"UInt","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorSMPTE\/documentation\/IvorSMPTE\/SMPTETi